  "body": "### What is the issue with the Compatibility Standard?\n\nDuring TPAC, the [WebExtensions Community Group](https://github.com/w3c/webextensions) agreed to coalesce around `window.browser` for a global namespace for extension APIs. Up until today, `window.chrome` is what is used in Chrome, and has been copied in other browsers. \r\n\r\n`window.browser` is already the canonical property in Firefox and Safari for extension APIs, and we at Chrome plan on aliasing  `window.chrome` to `window.browser`. In order to expose a new property on `window` in Chrome, we need to have it in a spec. As the WECG is a Community Group, we are not empowered to author specifications. We would like to add the `window.browser` as a property in the Compat spec as a User Agent defined property exposed for the use of Web Extension APIs.",
